{"_id":"68a7360f8ec3d8323af13298","nodeId":"aBjBHpq_OajgQjxdCobXD","roadmapSlug":"computer-science","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:54.940Z","description":"# Finding Hamiltonian Paths\n\nHamiltonian paths are paths that visit every node in a graph exactly once. They are named after the famous mathematician Hamilton. Hamiltonian paths are a special case of Hamiltonian cycles, which are cycles that visit every node in a graph exactly once.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Hamiltonian Cycles","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamiltonian_cycle","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3a98"},{"type":"article","title":"Hamiltonian Path","url":"https://www.hackerearth.com/practice/algorithms/graphs/hamiltonian-path/tutorial/","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3a99"},{"type":"article","title":"Hamiltonian Paths and Cycles","url":"https://medium.com/stamatics-iit-kanpur/hamiltonian-paths-and-cycles-4f233bfbc53a","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3a9a"},{"type":"article","title":"Hamiltonian Paths - Lecture 7","url":"https://people.csail.mit.edu/virgi/6.s078/lecture17.pdf","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3a9b"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:02:21.077Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/computer-science/content/aBjBHpq_OajgQjxdCobXD.md"}